    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">On Tuesday, May 19, 2015 at 1:56:43 PM UTC-4, Richard Erickson wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Model 3: includes model 2 plus a moving average for muPsi<div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">muPsi </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  alpha </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> tau </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> yearLessOne </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> epsilon</span></div></code></div></div><div>where </div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">  epsilon</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> normal</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sigmaEta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">year </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">nYears</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    epsilon</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">year</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> normal</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rho </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> epsilon</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">year </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sigmaEta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span></div></code></div></div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>This should usually be reparameterized as<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">parameters </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">nYears</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> z</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sigmaEta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// don&#39;t know why this has Eta in its symbol name</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">...</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">nYears</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> epsilon</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">nYears</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mu</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  epsilon</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sigmaEta </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> z</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span></div></code></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">year </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">nYears</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span></div></code></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    epsilon</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">year</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rho </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> epsilon</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">year </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sigmaEta </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> z</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">year</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  mu </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><code><span style=\"color:#000\">alpha </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> tau </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> yearLessOne </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> epsilon;</span></code>  </span><br><code><span style=\"color:#000\">  z </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> normal</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> // implies epsilon ~ normal(rho * epsilon[year - 1], sigmaEta)<br>  ...<br><br></span><span style=\"color:#000\"></span></code></div></code></div> </div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div></div><div>In this model, rho is not recoverable. Usually all or almost all of the epsilon parameter include 0 in their 80% CrI (see example output). I suspect this why Stan does not recover rho. Does this seem like a reasonable explanation?  <br></div></div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><br><div>You mean rho is not identifiable from the data alone? I don&#39;t immediately see why that would be. But I could see why there would be too much dependence between epsilon and sigmaEta to obtain good sampling the way you had it originally.<br><br>Ben<br><br><br></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
